{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138723-mokole-and-magi","id":1138723,"title":"Mokole and Magi?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-08T15:41:07-07:00","id":1138723,"title":"Mokole and Magi?","content":"I have always liked Mage and I have always like the Mokole, so is their any reason the two groups would get along and work together? I know WoD isn't supposed to be Super Friends, but how likely is it that the Mokole and different Mage Traditions have a relatively good rapport and a long tradition of exchanging services? Mages have to get their secret and forbidden histories from somewhere, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T15:55:14-07:00","id":1138732,"title":"","content":"I've had Australian Dreamspeakers in the past have good relationships with native Mokole, tbh with their long memories they know how bad Mages can be. Caerns become nodes to mages, and they arent often fond of sharing just like garou arent. Something I do remember from my above example, dreamspeaker found the mokole by traveling the Dreamtime and found the slumbering lizard under a mound. It became his mentor if I remember right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T16:03:43-07:00","id":1138734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freederp92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138723-mokole-and-magi?p=1138732#post1138732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had Australian Dreamspeakers in the past have good relationships with native Mokole, tbh with their long memories they know how bad Mages can be. Caerns become nodes to mages, and they arent often fond of sharing just like garou arent. Something I do remember from my above example, dreamspeaker found the mokole by traveling the Dreamtime and found the slumbering lizard under a mound. It became his mentor if I remember right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it. One of the reasons I ask is because I've read that the Hermetics were forced to fight alongside the Sidhe during the Accordence War because of long standing treaties and oaths that the Hermetics had completely forgotten about but the Sidhe held them to. I figure the Hermetics likely could figure out how useful the Mokole could be and made similar treaties. Hell, any of the Traditions could figure out that the Mokole were useful except maybe the Chorus. And even they might want to pick their brains in search of some evidence of The One.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T17:00:00-07:00","id":1138751,"title":"","content":"The Mokole book makes a passing comment about the Hem-ka Sobek (a group of mages) who worshiped Mokole as gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 09-09-2017, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T18:04:46-07:00","id":1138766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138723-mokole-and-magi?p=1138734#post1138734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like it. One of the reasons I ask is because I've read that the Hermetics were forced to fight alongside the Sidhe during the Accordence War because of long standing treaties and oaths that the Hermetics had completely forgotten about but the Sidhe held them to. I figure the Hermetics likely could figure out how useful the Mokole could be and made similar treaties. Hell, any of the Traditions could figure out that the Mokole were useful except maybe the Chorus. And even they might want to pick their brains in search of some evidence of The One.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhh remember few of the traditions deal with Fera and Garou. The Akashic Brotherhood might know of a Zhong Lung but if it pays them any mind is a different story. Dreamspeakers, and more nature and primal oriented traditions might have a contact among fera either as kinfolk or straight powerful contact. I remember playing with someone who was a bayou orphan outside New Orleans. He did voodoo and instinctual magic, protected gators from the enemies. He has a mokole companion per merit who woke up occasionally when something horrible happened or he needed wisdom.<br /> <br /> I see mokole as mentors mostly to Magi who respect nature","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T20:44:41-07:00","id":1138789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freederp92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138723-mokole-and-magi?p=1138766#post1138766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ehhh remember few of the traditions deal with Fera and Garou. The Akashic Brotherhood might know of a Zhong Lung but if it pays them any mind is a different story. Dreamspeakers, and more nature and primal oriented traditions might have a contact among fera either as kinfolk or straight powerful contact. I remember playing with someone who was a bayou orphan outside New Orleans. He did voodoo and instinctual magic, protected gators from the enemies. He has a mokole companion per merit who woke up occasionally when something horrible happened or he needed wisdom.<br /> <br /> I see mokole as mentors mostly to Magi who respect nature</div> </div> </div> </div>The Garou hate the Magi as being on the wrong side of their holy war to destroy things that defy Gaia's will, but I seem to remember that the other Fera had a more flexible view of Magi. I'm just speculating how likely it is that the Mokole and Magi could be presented as being a bit on the chummy side, a little like the Fianna and the Fae, or the White Howlers and the dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T21:36:38-07:00","id":1138798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138723-mokole-and-magi?p=1138789#post1138789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Garou hate the Magi as being on the wrong side of their holy war to destroy things that defy Gaia's will, but I seem to remember that the other Fera had a more flexible view of Magi. I'm just speculating how likely it is that the Mokole and Magi could be presented as being a bit on the chummy side, a little like the Fianna and the Fae, or the White Howlers and the dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>White Howlers and the dead? You must mean silent striders. It's possible mokole could be chummy with a few traditions. Akashic Brotherhood with the Zhong Lung, a Etherite might find a mokole simply interesting and form a hypothesis that he is from hollow earth or has a etherite help a mokole go to Hollow Eath because his latest mnesis quest lead him to find the last place the saurians dwell, actually what if the remains of the Dinosaur Kings have degenerate descendants in HE? I don't see VAs dealing much with mokole because of their tech orientation, also CC might seek them for their memories alone. Why wouldn't you ask something that's memory stretches almost all of creation? I can probably come up with more ideas on this topic.<br /> <br /> A few Disparate Alliance Magi can also form bonds with mokole. A Kahuna might ally himself with a aquatic mokole, asianic Magi Have strange relations with mokole since the ones they know are the Zhong Lung and just as much as the other mokole their spawn rate dwindles so many mokole are older specimens, usually stuck in their deep sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T23:41:45-07:00","id":1138812,"title":"","content":"Wu Lung tread carefully around the Zhong Lung*, according to Dragons of the East, because offending one means offending all of the Mokole's ancestors. Their paradigm frowns on this sort of rude behavior. To the extent that the Revised-era Akashayana had to buddy up with the Dragon Wizards, that advice about some people they've never met is about how much contact the Akashics would have with Mokole, aside from occasional astral jaunts where they saw a dinosaur dragon whizzing around memory realms and tuned it out. Given the Mage primacy of human belief and Werewolf's dismissal of them, the Mind-splat from Mage probably would not mesh well with the Memory of Gaia, who have been around the block and remember a time before there were primates, much less humans, and might have actually shaped human evolution with artificial selection on their part in an attempt to produce a being like their old Drachid kinfolk. The Mokole would likely also find the VAs insufferable for the Adepts' insistence that reality is a simulation and everything is data, but then, most other mages probably feel that way, too.<br /> <br /> Hollow Earth is not often mentioned in Werewolf, which has Pangaea and the Legendary Realm to fit that bill.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*Writing this out feels wrong, as usual. It should be either Zhong Long or Chung Lung, not a mixture of two Romanizations!</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T09:32:23-07:00","id":1138910,"title":"","content":"They would likely LOVE Etherites when they learn about there contacts with alternate timelines and that they know of a world where the Dragon Kings were never wiped out. That was one Easter Egg that I liked in the Revised SoE book.<br /> <br /> Edit: though this would beg the question of whether they could breed with them. Also, I kind of wonder if they can breed with bygone dragons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 09-09-2017, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T13:03:24-07:00","id":1138974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138723-mokole-and-magi?p=1138910#post1138910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They would likely LOVE Etherites when they learn about there contacts with alternate timelines and that they know of a world where the Dragon Kings were never wiped out. That was one Easter Egg that I liked in the Revised SoE book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt even the Glass Walkers would like Etherites. Sure, they can contact it, but it's skeevy reality-warping that's going to feel utterly wrong to the Dragon Breed, like Mnetics managed to warp WonderWorking with a Nexus Crawler or worse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: though this would beg the question of whether they could breed with them. Also, I kind of wonder if they can breed with bygone dragons. </div> </div> </div>Bygones aren't Bygones in Werewolf (and the cosmological assumptions of Werewolf violently disagree with the concept, since Thunderwyrms and Vhujunka need no Quint and suffer no Paradox), but they could be spirits. Breeding with spirits isn't just possible, it's how the John North Wind's Son, the Wendigo sig for Revised, came about. His name is extremely literal, as it turns out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T18:58:07-07:00","id":1139068,"title":"","content":"In general, the opinion of every Changing Breed (Garou + Fera), is that Mages are, at best, a bunch of hubristic monkeys fooling around with forces they shouldn't be allowed near. Sort of like small children getting a hold of handguns. <br /> <br /> That said, individual opinions will vary, and it's really going to depend on a number of factors, not least of which is the Tradition/paradigm/style of the Mage and the breed/tribe/background of the Werebeast. <br /> <br /> In East Asia, the Beast Courts and the local Awakened (Traditions + Crafts) hold each other at arm's length through several centuries of diplomatic etiquette and traditions. (Dragons of the East for Mage goes into more specific details.) But most Mages of any sort of traditional (small t) bent will look upon the Mokole with respect, if not out right awe, as they are 1) dragons, which makes them a big deal in the celestial hierarchy, and 2) are known to carry the memories of their illustrious ancestors (so any disrespect on your part will reflect poorly on both your own ancestors, but also your decedents down the line). The Wu Lung are especially hung up on this, but it also applies to regional Akashics, Dreamspeakers, and Ecstatics, among others. <br /> <br /> I don't pretend to be an expert on Australia, but to local Mages, especially Dreamspeakers or others of Aboriginal decent, the local Mokole and their ancestral memories offer a unique opportunity to connect with their own people's past, including parts that may be lost or in danger of being forgotten. Still, it's the sort of thing that is going to require a massive effort in diplomacy, perhaps over years if not decades or more, to create the sort of trust needed for such a thing. (This is compounded by the fact that both groups likely view themselves as members of completely separate mystic/religious societies, and sharing group secrets with outsiders is usually a major taboo.)<br /> <br /> With India, again, I'm not an expert, but the Makara are likely held in a somewhat quasi-divine status similar to that of the Middle Kingdom. If you decide to put supernaturals into a caste system, they are likely near the top, and there are undoubtably a ton of cultural and spiritual rules of etiquette and taboo when it comes to dealing with them. Various Hindu factions of Mages, including Thanatoics, Ecstatics, Celestials, and Dreamspeakers, probably have centuries of diplomatic protocols for interacting with Mokole. <br /> <br /> In Africa and South America, the Mokole and Dreamspeakers are likely aware of each other, but again, they probably give each other a wide berth. Likewise in Egypt with the Web of Faith, Batini, Dreamspeakers, and others. <br /> <br /> In the Caribbean and Gulf Coast, you've got various Voodoo oriented Mages (Bata'a, Dreamspeakers, Thanatoics, Ecstatics, Verbena, etc.) who run in similar circles of homid Mokole in the same region, but as with all the others, there's probably an unspoken rule of leaving each other alone. (You especially never, ever, go near a Mokole breeding ground; that's just asking to become dinosaur chow.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T19:14:54-07:00","id":1139073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138723-mokole-and-magi?p=1138974#post1138974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt even the Glass Walkers would like Etherites.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Umbral Fliers camp of the Glass Walkers are actually supposed to be - or at least were - pulp style adventurers of the 20s and 30s, the likes of G-8 and his Battle Aces, Connie Kurridge, Buck Rodgers, Flash Gordon and Doc Savage. After WW2, the bulk of them decided the world had passed them by and went to explore the deeper regions of the Umbra. I like to think that the modern ones remaining on earth are doing weird blends of SETI, UFO chasing, parapsychology, time travel experiments and space exploration. But if you want to do a Pulp Era crossover between Werewolf and Mage, they are a lot of fun for that. (There is, IIRC, Werewolf's Pulp Era signature pack statted out on the book Past Lives.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T19:43:43-07:00","id":1139076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138723-mokole-and-magi?p=1138910#post1138910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They would likely LOVE Etherites when they learn about there contacts with alternate timelines and that they know of a world where the Dragon Kings were never wiped out. That was one Easter Egg that I liked in the Revised SoE book.<br /> <br /> Edit: though this would beg the question of whether they could breed with them. Also, I kind of wonder if they can breed with bygone dragons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say its an Easter Egg vs Parallel lines of development. The Muvians and Dragon Kings are both Dinosaur people. They are not the same dinosaur people. Just like the Hollow Earth is part of the High Umbra.<br /> <br /> And crosstime travel is pretty explicit that you can't bring items back between timelines without expenditure of equal resources thus why the Technocracy doesn't just get help from a timeline where they are much better off.<br /> <br /> That being said I imagine the interactions between a Mokole and Etherite are pretty much up to the Etherite. The Etherites are perhaps the least cohesive Tradition out there, you might have ones who practice sciences of various ancient species that the Mokole remember and can play off eachother, you might have an etherite solidly into biotech or even one that looks for all intents and purposes like a Dreamspeaker but knows there's a &quot;science&quot; behind engagement with extradimensional beings(see the Scientific Mystic merit)<br /> <br /> Really as long as the Etherite isn't a jackass things should work out.. of course ALOT of mages are Jackasses..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T22:47:54-07:00","id":1139107,"title":"","content":"In truth, it's not very clear *where* Hollow Earth it's. Sometimes it's insinuated that it's located in the Shard Realm of Matter...This would locate it on the Deep Umbra.<br /> <br /> Actually I think that makes a lot more sense than the Astral Umbra for various reasons:<br /> One, because old days Hollow Earth (that's the only hollow earth because the place was never explored after the Book of Worlds) was material in nature: That is, it's inhabitants and stuff weren't made of Ephemera (Matter Sphere works as normal). This makes little sense for the Astral, but a lot for Matter.<br /> <br /> Two, because it's not mentioned in Astral Umbra sections. Astral travel it's not the usual way to get there. There's no indication that it's creatures think that a physical traveler &quot;it's weird&quot;, like there is when you Spirit 3 to the Astral. There's no known portal from there to the Vulgate nor to Spires. (In fact, because the place isn't ephemeral, the astral form shouldn't be able to interact with it without an anchor of some kind)<br /> <br /> Three: The old way (that wasn't retconned, but rather blown by the Storm) of accessing Hollow Earth was using deep tunels. This resembles how the Deep Umbra can be accessed by stepping sideways in Mariana's Trench, a very deep place-who can say if entering a volcanoe or a very deep hole in Antartica (and surviving) isn't another place where the Deep touches Earth? (that leaves you on Matter)<br /> <br /> But the correspondences that this place may have with what Mokole are (with the real past) it's something that the ST would have to decide...<br /> <br /> Another thing it's the Dream background. It isn't what the Mokole do...but the ST could declare that Dream has something to do with Mokole turf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-10-2017, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T22:58:39-07:00","id":1139111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138723-mokole-and-magi?p=1139107#post1139107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In truth, it's not very clear *where* Hollow Earth it's. Sometimes it's insinuated that it's located in the Shard Realm of Matter...This would locate it on the Deep Umbra.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Seems reasonable enough, I just don't think its Pangea or any other realm generally used in W:TA by another name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T23:38:55-07:00","id":1139113,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you're right about that, they aren't related. I think Pangea it's even mentioned in the Book of worlds as a place where werewolves go, it's never related to Hollow Earth as far as I remember, nor to the memory of Gaia.<br /> <br /> Albeit I may be open to the idea that one realm could have a portal that leads to the other, much like Astral Hell may have a portal to Malfeas and portals exist between various places and the Dark Umbra. This may be the seed of a story (mage/lizard traverses the wrong door, which closes: now they are trapped in an alien place and need the help of the locals to get out, which may include helping/facing a member of the other splat)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T09:37:53-07:00","id":1139220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138723-mokole-and-magi#post1138723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always liked Mage and I have always like the Mokole, so is their any reason the two groups would get along and work together? I know WoD isn't supposed to be Super Friends, but how likely is it that the Mokole and different Mage Traditions have a relatively good rapport and a long tradition of exchanging services? Mages have to get their secret and forbidden histories from somewhere, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the Breedbook, Mokole consider Kin to be an Auspice of their own. (8th Sun). In some cases (not all), Awakened and other 'enhanced' Kinfolk are given Auspice titles and deed names. The opening comic of the Breedbook contains a Shaman Kin that has been declared 'Crowned', which is a leadership title.<br /> <br /> Mokole as keepers of knowledge and memory place a <i>high</i> value on Kin with extrodinary abilities, even compared to the mystically inclined Bastet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T11:13:31-07:00","id":1139233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138723-mokole-and-magi?p=1139220#post1139220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to the Breedbook, Mokole consider Kin to be an Auspice of their own. (8th Sun). In some cases (not all), Awakened and other 'enhanced' Kinfolk are given Auspice titles and deed names. The opening comic of the Breedbook contains a Shaman Kin that has been declared 'Crowned', which is a leadership title.<br /> <br /> Mokole as keepers of knowledge and memory place a <i>high</i> value on Kin with extrodinary abilities, even compared to the mystically inclined Bastet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. I also seem to remember that Mages make extraordinary breeding stock. I can imagine that the Mokole, reduced greatly in number, might have made a deal with some cabals, trading knowledge and connections with the spirit world in exchange for an infusion of strong, magical blood that probably can produce all sorts of supernatural merits. From there, all sorts of ties and oaths could be sworn. <br /> <br /> Marriages and children have long been tools used to end feuds and forge alliances. This could be a means to forge inroads between Magi and Changing Breeds that were driven to near extinction. Magi are always lamenting the loss of magic and this could have been a good way for them to protect magic at one point and make some allies at a point in their history when they would've shaken hands with the Wyrm himself for aid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 09-10-2017, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T12:29:19-07:00","id":1139246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138723-mokole-and-magi?p=1139073#post1139073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Umbral Fliers camp of the Glass Walkers are actually supposed to be - or at least were - pulp style adventurers of the 20s and 30s, the likes of G-8 and his Battle Aces, Connie Kurridge, Buck Rodgers, Flash Gordon and Doc Savage. After WW2, the bulk of them decided the world had passed them by and went to explore the deeper regions of the Umbra. I like to think that the modern ones remaining on earth are doing weird blends of SETI, UFO chasing, parapsychology, time travel experiments and space exploration. But if you want to do a Pulp Era crossover between Werewolf and Mage, they are a lot of fun for that. (There is, IIRC, Werewolf's Pulp Era signature pack statted out on the book Past Lives.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoth the narrator of the Revised Tribebook, &quot;Please don't join them. Let them die; I don't enjoy talking about them.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T15:01:25-07:00","id":1139282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138723-mokole-and-magi?p=1139233#post1139233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cool. I also seem to remember that Mages make extraordinary breeding stock. I can imagine that the Mokole, reduced greatly in number, might have made a deal with some cabals, trading knowledge and connections with the spirit world in exchange for an infusion of strong, magical blood that probably can produce all sorts of supernatural merits. From there, all sorts of ties and oaths could be sworn.<br /> <br /> Marriages and children have long been tools used to end feuds and forge alliances. This could be a means to forge inroads between Magi and Changing Breeds that were driven to near extinction. Magi are always lamenting the loss of magic and this could have been a good way for them to protect magic at one point and make some allies at a point in their history when they would've shaken hands with the Wyrm himself for aid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personal Headcanon would be that's why the Zhong Lung are so different from their fellow Mokole including having superior longevity Gifts...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T16:20:27-07:00","id":1139299,"title":"","content":"Gift? Not rites that any Mokole could learn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T18:03:47-07:00","id":1139310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138723-mokole-and-magi?p=1139299#post1139299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gift? Not rites that any Mokole could learn?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Zhong Lung have on their gift list exchange Gnosis for 12 extra years of life. Its repeatable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T18:38:46-07:00","id":1139324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138723-mokole-and-magi?p=1139246#post1139246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quoth the narrator of the Revised Tribebook, &quot;Please don't join them. Let them die; I don't enjoy talking about them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. To modern Glasswalkers, they're almost as weird and unpractical as the maybe half-dozen of the tribe who still practice alchemy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T19:41:50-07:00","id":1139335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138723-mokole-and-magi?p=1139310#post1139310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Zhong Lung have on their gift list exchange Gnosis for 12 extra years of life. Its repeatable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this 20 or before? I definitely remember pushing out bones while expending permanent gnosis as a rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T08:06:58-07:00","id":1139711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. To modern Glasswalkers, they're almost as weird and unpractical as the maybe half-dozen of the tribe who still practice alchemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deemed as &quot;weird and unpractical&quot;, and shunned by the Tribe...sounds like the kind of Garou that would make good buddies for Etherites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T18:04:49-07:00","id":1139799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138723-mokole-and-magi?p=1139711#post1139711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deemed as &quot;weird and unpractical&quot;, and shunned by the Tribe...sounds like the kind of Garou that would make good buddies for Etherites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, &quot;buddies&quot; is a subjective term when it comes to various supernaturals (there's a reason the revised Silent Striders version of Vik Striker gives him a full pack - including the Glasswalker Dr. Stratos, Australian Garou of SCIENCE! - in place of the Etherite and Eshu associates he had in the original), but, yes, they make really suitable potential contacts, friendly rivals, or other encounters for Etherjammers in a Mage/W